# DRY, KISS, and separation of concerns

Do not copy a behavior that already exists. Share the mechanism once. Keep each file to one job. Prefer the smallest change that matches an existing helper.

## DRY

- A second copy of the same branch, mapper, or request flow belongs in `shared/` (apps) or the owning lib (libs), not in another page file.
- Resource-specific text stays at the call site. Shared code takes that text as data.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — same status switch in every page
if (error instanceof ApiError) {
  switch (error.status) {
    case 401:
      return 'Your session has expired. Sign in again.';
  }
}

// ✅ GOOD
describeCatalogError(error, { forbidden, notFound, conflict, invalid, unreachable });
```

## KISS

- One function, one obvious path. No extra wrapper, flag, or layer unless a second caller needs it.
- Do not generalize a helper for a case that does not exist yet.

## Separation of concerns

- Wire shapes stay in `@cms/<mfe>-contract`. Fetch and cache stay in data-access. Screens stay in the page.
- A page file names its resource. It does not reimplement transport, status mapping, or another page's layout.
